{
  "name": "Webhook Data Tables Combine Multiple Chat Messages into One",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "b1-1",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -760,
        -440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### How it works\n1. **Receive Chat Message** stores each message (`sender_id`, `text`) in a Data Table.\n2. After `debounce_seconds` only the newest message's run goes on, unless the oldest waited `max_wait_seconds`.\n3. **Claim Batch** marks up to `max_messages` unmarked rows, oldest first, in one update, so each message joins one batch; full batches go at once.\n4. Your bot gets the texts in arrival order; delivered rows are deleted. **Retry Every 30 Minutes** resends failed batches; after `max_attempts` one is parked, failing the run for your error workflow.\n\n### Setup\n1. Execute **Run Once to Create Buffer Table** (needs data table create permission).\n2. Attach a Header Auth credential to **Receive Chat Message**.\n3. In your chat workflow, replace the bot with an HTTP Request node POSTing JSON `sender_id` and `text` with that header to the Production URL.\n4. Start your bot sub-workflow with a copy of **When Batch Is Ready (Example Bot)**, publish it and put its id in `bot_workflow_id` (empty runs the example).\n5. In **Buffer Settings** check `buffer_table_name`, `debounce_seconds`, `max_wait_seconds`, `max_messages`, `max_text_length`, `max_attempts`, `retry_after_seconds` (keep it above max wait + debounce). Times are UTC.\n6. Optionally set an error workflow in Workflow Settings. Activate.\n\nCost: one execution per message plus 48 retry runs a day.\n\n### Customization\nEdit the joiner in **Build Combined Message**.\n\nLimits: without locks, two runs may split a burst into two batches, never a message into both. Messages arriving while your bot works form the next batch, which can run alongside it and may be answered first. If releasing or clearing fails, the run fails and rows keep their `batch_id` (not resent; delivered rows stay).",
        "width": 660,
        "height": 1340
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b1-2",
      "name": "Setup Section",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## One-time setup\nCreates the buffer Data Table with its six columns (skipped if it exists). Tested on n8n 2.47.7.",
        "width": 920,
        "height": 300,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b1-3",
      "name": "Receive Section",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -100
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Receive and store\nn8n answers 403 without the header secret. Checks `sender_id` and `text` (400 if missing or blank), finds the table by its exact name (503 if missing), stores the message and answers 202 (500 if storing fails).",
        "width": 2440,
        "height": 460,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b1-4",
      "name": "Debounce Section",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2420,
        -100
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Wait for a quiet moment\nAfter `debounce_seconds` only the newest message's run goes on, unless the oldest is `max_wait_seconds` old. Full batches of `max_messages` go at once; a smaller rest waits by these rules.",
        "width": 1120,
        "height": 460,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b1-5",
      "name": "Retry Section",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        400
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Retry every 30 minutes\nTakes messages still unclaimed after `retry_after_seconds` (keep it above max wait + debounce, or a burst can go early): released after a bot failure, or left by a run lost in a restart. Batches per sender, at most `max_messages` each.",
        "width": 2160,
        "height": 340,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b1-6",
      "name": "Deliver Section",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3580,
        -100
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Claim, combine, deliver\nOne update claims only unclaimed rows. Your bot gets the batch; delivered rows are deleted, failed ones released for retry or parked after `max_attempts`, which fails the run. To resend a parked (`parked-` prefix) or stuck (old, non-empty `batch_id`) batch, clear its `batch_id`.",
        "width": 2200,
        "height": 840,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b1-7",
      "name": "Example Bot Section",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3580,
        780
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Example bot (input contract)\nYour bot sub-workflow starts with these inputs. `sender_id` tells it whom to answer. Replace **Example Bot Reply** with your bot and reply from there. A batch fails only if this workflow errors (or outputs just an `error` field).",
        "width": 900,
        "height": 360,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
